<objdefs appVersion="1.0.12">
   <obj.normal id="165ctrl v" uuid="0c9bfe43-cf10-4cf6-8d85-096f6c56f8d1">
      <sDescription>External digital input pin control
"v" version: variable rate control.
Tie "CLK INH" / clock inhibit pin to GND.
Pins updated for Ksoloti Core.
Data input. Also called SER, SDAT, DS... Usually pin 10 on the HC165.
Clock output. Also called CLK, SCLK, CP... Usually pin 2 on the HC165.
Latch output. Also called SH/LD, PL... Usually pin 1 on the HC165.
If you want to chain HC165's (up to 4), you need to forward the serial data via the QH (also called Q7) pins.
Connect the first 165's 'QH' pin (9) to the second 165's 'SER' pin (10), and so on.
</sDescription>
      <author>Ricard Wanderlof, Ksoloti</author>
      <license>BSD</license>
